Spec: Invoice Demo Fixture

Platform: Python 3

Purpose:
  Provide a small plausible code project for exercising SpecDD language support.
  Keep the fixture simple enough to inspect while still using realistic source-adjacent specs.

Structure:
  ./app.sdd: Fixture project contract.
  ./src/invoice_demo: Python package for invoice creation and storage.
  ./src/invoice_demo/module.sdd: Package-level implementation contract.
  ./src/invoice_demo/models.py: Domain model definitions.
  ./src/invoice_demo/models.sdd: Domain model contract.
  ./src/invoice_demo/repository.py: In-memory invoice repository.
  ./src/invoice_demo/repository.sdd: Repository contract.
  ./src/invoice_demo/service.py: Invoice service orchestration.
  ./src/invoice_demo/service.sdd: Service contract.
  ./src/invoice_demo/cli.py: Minimal command-line adapter.
  ./src/invoice_demo/cli.sdd: CLI adapter contract.
  ./tests/test_service.py: Service behavior tests.
  ./tests/test_service.sdd: Service test contract.
  ./kitchen-sink.sdd: Full language coverage fixture.
  ./kitchen-sink-invalid.sdd: Deliberately invalid language diagnostics fixture.

Owns:
  ./src/invoice_demo/*
  ./tests/*
  ./kitchen-sink.sdd
  ./kitchen-sink-invalid.sdd

Can modify:
  ./src/invoice_demo/*
  ./tests/*
  ./kitchen-sink.sdd
  ./kitchen-sink-invalid.sdd

Can read:
  /README.md
  ./src/invoice_demo/*.py
  ./src/invoice_demo/*.sdd
  ./tests/*.py
  ./tests/*.sdd

References:
  ./src/invoice_demo/service.py
  ./src/invoice_demo/service.sdd
  ./tests/test_service.py
  ./tests/test_service.sdd

Must:
  Keep the sample project dependency-free.
  Keep source files small and readable.
  Use explicit path prefixes for file and glob references.
  Use explicit `@` prefixes for symbol references.
  Keep positive fixture specs valid under the formal SpecDD language rules.
  Keep ./kitchen-sink-invalid.sdd intentionally invalid for diagnostics coverage.

Must not:
  Add packaging metadata, dependency managers, or generated files.
  Use network access, clocks, randomness, or external persistence.

Depends on:
  Python standard library
  @invoice_demo.service.InvoiceService
  @invoice_demo.repository.InvoiceRepository

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Add a minimal invoice domain model.
  [x] #2 Add an in-memory repository.
  [x] #3 Add service orchestration.
  [x] #4 Add service tests and adjacent specs.
  [ ] #5 Keep future fixture changes aligned with `/fixtures/README.md`.

Scenario: invoice creation succeeds
  Given a customer id and one positive invoice line
  When @invoice_demo.service.InvoiceService.create_invoice creates the invoice
  Then the returned invoice has a total greater than zero
  And ./tests/test_service.py can verify the behavior

Example: project-root references
  source glob: ./src/invoice_demo/*.py
  spec glob: ./src/invoice_demo/*.sdd
